  "body": "Supersedes #889\r\nRelated to https://github.com/gkjohnson/three-gpu-pathtracer/issues/769, #884\r\nFix #283 \r\n\r\nAdds a \"ClusteredBVH\" class for compute specifically that takes a set of objects with BVHs and groups the BVH nodes rather than object nodes to reduce TLAS bounds overlaps.\r\n\r\nFor three-gpu-pathtracer this brings the rover model rendering up from ~50fps to ~100fps\r\n\r\n**TODO**\r\n- Determine API surface (not public for now)\r\n- Review\r\n\r\n**Later**\r\n- Add a guard to for depth\r\n- Share more code between ObjectBVH, ClusteredMetaBVH?\r\n- Test / improve build perf, refit\r\n- Clustering based on overlap would be best\r\n- Cache inner leaf sizes to improve BVH traversal time\r\n- Consider whether we should use a \"tight\" bounding volume (eg collapsed to inner primitives?) - test whether perf is good enough\r\n  - Or just tighten by the parent precise AABB - but requires caching the parent bounds",
